          %title Basic Homotopy Theory
          %hr/
          %p
            This page (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/IntroductionToTopologyII-170720.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            and the induced concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of a topological space, the first step in extracting combinatorial data in homotopy theory. We use this example to introduce
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            in general and mention that this models the homotopy theory of those topological spaces that are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-types"} homotopy 1-types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
            and use groupoids to give a simple proof of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            and has many applications. As one example application, we use it to prove that the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+the+circle+is+the+integers"} fundamental group of the circle is the integers
          %p
