                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"}> homotopy hypothesis
                        \-theorem
          %h1#basic_homotopy_theory Basic Homotopy Theory
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Homotopy"} Homotopy
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#FundamentalGroups"} Fundamental group
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#Groupoid"} Groupoids
              %li
                %a{:href => "#CoveringSpaces"} Covering spaces
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#lifting_properties"} Lifting properties
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#Monodromy"} Monodromy
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ExamplesFundamentalGroups"} Fundamental groups
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HigherHomotopyGroups"} Higher homotopy groups
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In order to handle topological spaces, to compute their properties and to distinguish them, it turns out to be useful to consider not just continuous variation within a topological space, i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            between topological spaces, but also continuous deformations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            themselves. This is the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
            below), and its study is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of continuous functions between them then their nature changes, and one speaks of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            (remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IsomorphismHomotopyEquivalence"}
            below).
          %p
            Of particular interest are homotopies between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
            in a topological space. If a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop"} loop
            in a topological space is homotopic to the constant loop, this means that it does not “wind around a hole” in the space. Hence the set of homotopy classes of loops in a topological space, which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concatenation+of+paths"} concatenation of paths
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of the space (def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalGroupoidAndFundamentalGroup"}
          %p
            This same information turns out to be encoded in “continuously varying sets” over a topological space, hence in “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
            of
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringSpace"}
            below). As one moves around a loop, then the parameterized set comes back to itself up to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            of the loop. This encodes an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            of the fundamental group. The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalTheoremOfCoveringSpaces"}
            below) says that covering spaces are equivalently characterized by their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of the fundamental group. This is an incarnation of the general principle of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+the+circle+is+the+integers"} fundamental group of the circle is the integers
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CircleFundamentalGroup"}
            below).
          %p
            In order to formulate and prove these statements, it turns out convenient to do away with the arbitrary choice of basepoint that is involved in the definition of fundamental groups, and instead collect
            %em all
            homotopy classes of paths into a single structure, called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of a topological space (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalGroupoid"}
            below) an example of a generalization of groups to
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            (discussed
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Groupoid"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            incarnation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            presented by a topological space,
            %em up to level 1
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-type"} homotopy 1-type
          %p
            The algebraic reflection of the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of a topological space involves higher dimensional analogs for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                higher
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HigherHomotopyGroups"} below
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#Homotopy Homotopy
          %p
            It is clear that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            or equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_0^\circ(1)
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            is
            %em not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast = \mathbb{R}^0
            (simply because there is not even a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between the underlying
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            = succeed "-ball" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-ball" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            This intuition is made precise by observing that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Topology+--+1#BinaryProductTopologicalSpace"}> this example
            ) of the open ball with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\eta \colon [0,1] \times B_0^\circ(1)  \longrightarrow B_0^\circ(1)
          %p which is given by rescaling:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (t,x) \mapsto t \cdot x
                  \\,.
          %p
            This continuously interpolates between the open ball and the point, in that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 1
            it restricts to the identity, while for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 0
            it restricts to the map constant on the origin.
          %p
            We may summarize this situation by saying that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi B
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ∘
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∃
                              %mo !
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi const
                                  %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ×
                          %msubsup
                            %mi B
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ∘
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo ,
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↦
                              %mi t
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi B
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ∘
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi B
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ∘
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  B_0^\circ(1) \times \{0\} &amp;\overset{\exists !}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{const_0}}
                  \\\
                  [0,1] \times B_0^\circ(1)
                  \&amp;\overset{(t,x) \mapsto t \cdot x}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  B^\circ_0(1)
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\simeq}
                  \\\
                  B_0^\circ(1) \times \{1\}
                  }
          %p
            Such “continuous deformations” are called
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
          %p In the following we use this terminology:
          #TopologicalInterval.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+interval"}> topological interval
                )
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+interval"} topological interval
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1] \subset \mathbb{R}^1
                  regarded as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  in the standard way, as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
                  with its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi const
                              %mn 0
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo *
                            %mo →
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const_0 \;\colon\; \ast \to [0,1]
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi const
                              %mn 1
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo *
                            %mo →
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const_1 \;\colon\; \ast \to [0,1]
                %p
                  which include the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
                  as the two endpoints, respectively
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with the (unique)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [0,1] \overset{}{\longrightarrow} \ast
                %p
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
                  (which is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %p regarded, in summary, as a factorization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi const
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi const
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\nabla_\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\ast \sqcup \ast
                    \\overset{(const_0,const_1)}{\longrightarrow}
                    [0,1]
                    \\overset{}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\ast
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
              on the point space, namely the unique continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_\ast
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \sqcup \ast \simeq Disc(\{0,1\})
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+space"} discrete topological space
              on two elements).
          #LeftHomotopy.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"}> homotopy
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              be two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f,g\colon X \longrightarrow Y
            %p
              be two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              between them.
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} (left)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; f \,\Rightarrow\, g
                    \\,,
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; X \times [0,1] \longrightarrow Y
            %p
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Topology+--+1#BinaryProductTopologicalSpace"}> this example
              ) of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+interval"} topological interval
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalInterval"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commute
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AHomotopy.jpg", :width => "400"}/
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\{0\} \times X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id,const_0)}}\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    X \times [0,1]  &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id,const_1)}}\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    \\{1\} \times X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %blockquote
              %p
                graphics grabbed from J. Tauber
                %a{:href => "http://jtauber.com/blog/2005/07/01/path_homotopy/"} here
            %p hence such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mtext and
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta(-,0) = f
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\text{and}
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\eta(-,1) = g
                    \\,.
            %p
              If there is a homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow g
              (possibly unspecified) we say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
              %em homotopic
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi h
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \sim_h g
                    \\,.
          #EquivRelHomotopy.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                is an
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              be two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{Top}(X,Y)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              Then the relating of being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              on this set. The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X,Y] \; \coloneqq \; Hom_{Top}(X,Y)/\sim_h
            %p
              is called the set of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of continuous functions.
            %p
              Moreover, this equivalence relation is compatible with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of continuous functions:
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y,Z \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              three topological spaces, there is a unique function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X,Y] \times [Y,Z] \longrightarrow [X,Z]
            %p
              such that the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Top
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Top
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi Y
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Top
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{Top}(X,Y) \times Hom_{Top}(Y,Z)
                    \&amp;\overset{\circ_{X,Y,Z}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Hom_{Top}(X,Z)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{}}
                    \\\
                    [X,Y] \times [Y,Z] &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; [X,Z]
                    }
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To see that the relation is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow f
              from a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to itself is given by the function which is constant on the topological interval:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 1
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \times [0,1] \overset{pr_1}{\longrightarrow} X
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is continuous because
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projections"} projections
              out of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
              are continuous, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %p
              To see that the relation is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"} symmetric
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon f \Rightarrow g
              is a homotopy then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi id
                                  %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \times [0,1] &amp;\overset{id_X \times (1-(-))}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X \times [0,1] &amp;\overset{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    (x,t) &amp;\mapsto&amp; (x,1-t) &amp;\mapsto&amp;  \eta(x,1-t)
                    }
            %p
              is a homotopy
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \Rightarrow f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1-(-)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
              function, and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials+are+continuous"} polynomials are continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of continuous functions is again continuous.
            %p
              Finally to see that the relation is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_1 \colon f \Rightarrow g
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_2 \colon g \Rightarrow h
              are two composable homotopies, then consider the “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              \-parameterized
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+concatenation"} path concatenation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo ∘
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %msub
                                        %mi η
                                        %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi x
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mn 2
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo ≤
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                      %mn 2
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %msub
                                        %mi η
                                        %mn 2
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi x
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mn 2
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo −
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo ≤
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \times [0,1] &amp;\overset{\eta_2 \circ \eta_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    (x,t) &amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\eta_1(x,2t) &amp;\vert&amp; t \leq 1/2
                    \\\
                    \\eta_{2}(x,2t-1) &amp;\vert&amp; t \leq 1/2
                    }
                    \\right.
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              To see that this is continuous, observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ X \times [0,1/2] \subset X, X \times [1/2,1] \subset X \}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times [0,1]
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
              (in the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topology"} product topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_1(-,2(-))
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_2(-,2(-)-1)
              are continuous (being composites of Cartesian products of continuous functions) and agree on the intersection
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times \{1/2\}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Top#ClosedSubspacesGluing"} this example
            %p Finally to see that homotopy respects composition: Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi Y
                            %munderover
                              %mrow
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ′
                                    %mn 2
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                            %mi Z
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 3
                            %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X
                    \\overset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}
                    Y
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{f'_2}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{f_2}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {}
                    Z
                    \\overset{f_3}{\longrightarrow}
                    W
                    }
            %p be continuous functions, and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; f_2 \Rightarrow f'_2
            %p be a homotopy. It is sufficient to show that then there is a homotopy of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_3 \circ f_2 \circ f_1 \Rightarrow   f_3 \circ f'_2 \circ f_1
                    \\,.
            %p This is exhibited by the following diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi X
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi Y
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msub
                                  %mi id
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                    %mn 0
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 3
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi X
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ′
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\overset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{ (id_X, const_0) }}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{ (id_Y,const_0) }}\downarrow
                    \&amp;
                    \\searrow^{\mathrlap{ f_2}}
                    \\\
                    X \times [0,1]
                    \&amp;\overset{f_1 \times id_{[0,1]} }{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y \times [0,1]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Z &amp;\overset{f_3}{\longrightarrow}&amp; W
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id_X,  const_1)}}\uparrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{ (id,const_1) } }\uparrow
                    \&amp;
                    \\nearrow_{\mathrlap{ f'_2 }}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\underset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
          #HomotopyCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"}> homotopy category
                )
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivRelHomotopy"}
              means that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are still the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %p
              This category (at least when restricted to spaces that admit the structure of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho(Top)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              topological spaces, then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Top
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{Ho(Top)}(X,Y) = [X,Y]
            %p
              Moreover, sending a continuous function to its homotopy class is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\kappa \;\colon\; Top \longrightarrow Ho(Top)
            %p
              from the ordinary category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of topological spaces with actual continuous functions between them.
          #HomotopyEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"}> homotopy equivalence
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              be two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Y
            %p
              is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              if there exists
            %ol
              %li
                %p a continuous function the other way around,
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g \;\colon\; Y \longrightarrow X
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f\circ g \Rightarrow id_Y
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g\circ f \Rightarrow id_X
                    \\,.
            %p We indicate that a continuous function is a homotopy equivalence by writing
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi h
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \overset{\simeq_h}{\longrightarrow} Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              If there exists
              %em some
              (possibly unspecified) homotopy equivalence between topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi h
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \simeq_h Y
                    \\,.
          #IsomorphismHomotopyEquivalence.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                in the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            %p
              In view of remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategory"}
              a continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a homotopy equivalence precisely if its image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa(f)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              As an object of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+homotopy+type"} strong
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              which
              %em present
              them, in that topological spaces that are far from being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              may still be equivalent as homotopy types.
          #HomotopyEquivalenceHomeomorphism.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyEquivalence"}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %p
              Being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This is immediate from remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IsomorphismHomotopyEquivalence"}
              by general properties of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %p
              But for the record we spell it out. This involves the construction already used in the proof of prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivRelHomotopy"}
            %p
              It is clear that the relation it
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"} symmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitive
              consider continuous functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                    %mi Y
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 2
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{g_1}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {}
                    Y
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{g_2}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{f_2}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {}
                    Z
            %p and homotopies
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_1 \circ f_1 \Rightarrow id_X
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    f_1 \circ g_1 \Rightarrow id_Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_2 \circ f_2 \Rightarrow id_Y
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    f_2 \circ g_2 \Rightarrow id_Z
                    \\,.
            %p We need to produce homotopies of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (g_1 \circ g_2 ) \circ (f_2 \circ f_1) \Rightarrow id_X
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_2 \circ f_1)  \circ (g_1 \circ g_2 )  \Rightarrow id_Y
                    \\,.
            %p Now the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi X
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi Y
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msub
                                  %mi id
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                    %mn 0
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi X
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi const
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\overset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{ (id_X, const_0) }}\downarrow &amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{(id_Y,const_0)}}\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{ g_2 \circ f_2}}
                    \\\
                    X \times [0,1] &amp;\overset{f_1 \times id_{[0,1]} }{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y \times [0,1]  &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y &amp;\overset{g_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id_X,  const_1)}}\uparrow &amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{(id,const_1)}}\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{ id_Y }}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\underset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              one of the given homotopies, exhibits a homotopy
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g_1\circ g_2) \circ (f_2 \circ f_1) \Rightarrow g_1 \circ f_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1 \circ f_1 \Rightarrow id_X
              gives the first of the two homotopies required above. The second one follows by the same construction, just with the labels of the functions exchanged.
          #SpaceContractible.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"}> contractible topological space
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
              if the unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \overset{\simeq_h}{\longrightarrow} \ast
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyEquivalence"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+spaces"} contractible topological spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+objects"} terminal objects
                in the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            %p
              In view of remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpaceContractible"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa(X)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          #BallIsContractible.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+ball"} closed ball
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^n \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              be the unit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+ball"} closed ball
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
              (def.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpaceContractible"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi h
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p \;\colon\; B^n \overset{\simeq_h}{\longrightarrow} \ast
                    \\,.
            %p The homotopy inverse function is necessarily constant on a point, we may just as well choose it to go pick the origin:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    const_0 \;\colon\; \ast \overset{}{\longrightarrow} B^n
                    \\,.
            %p
              For one way of composing these functions we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p \circ const_0 = id_\ast
            %p
              with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivRelHomotopy"}
            %p The other composite is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    const_0 \circ p = const_0 \;\colon\; B^n \overset{}{\longrightarrow} B^n
                    \\,.
            %p Hence we need to produce a homotopy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    const_0 \Rightarrow id_{B^n}
            %p This is given by the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B^n \times [0,1] &amp;\overset{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B^n
                    \\\
                    (x,t) &amp;\mapsto&amp; t x
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we use the multiplication with respect to the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              structure in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the whole
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Topology+--+1#OpenBallsHomeomorphicToRn"}> this example
              ) it follows with example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyEquivalenceHomeomorphism"}
              and example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivRelHomotopy"}
              that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              is a contractible topological space:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi h
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \overset{\simeq_h}{\longrightarrow} \ast
                    \\,.
          %p
            In direct generalization of the construction in example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BallIsContractible"}
            one finds further examples as follows:
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The following three
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphs"} graphs
            %p
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ThreeNonHomeoButHomotopyEquivGraphs.png", :width => "400"}/
            %p
              (i.e. the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspaces"} topological subspaces
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
              that these pictures indicate) are not
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
              with two points removed, by the homotopies indicated by the following pictures:
            %p
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HomotopyEquivalentsToBiAnnulus.png", :width => "400"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                graphics grabbed from
                %a{:href => "homotopy+equivalence#Hatcher"} Hatcher
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#FundamentalGroups Fundamental group
          #PathHomotopyRelativeBoundary.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"}> homotopy relative boundary
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma_1, \gamma_2 \;\colon\; [0,1] \longrightarrow X
            %p
              be two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma_1(0) = \gamma_2(0)
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    \\gamma_1(1) = \gamma_2(1)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"} homotopy relative boundary
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_1
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_2
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; \gamma_1 \Rightarrow \gamma_2
            %p such that it does not move the endpoints:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAAA
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta(0,-) = const_{\gamma_1(0)} = const_{\gamma_2(0)}
                    \\phantom{AAAAAA}
                    \\eta(1,-) = const_{\gamma_1(0)} = const_{\gamma_2(1)}
                    \\,.
          #EquivalenceRelationHomotopyRelativeBoundary.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"} homotopy relative boundary
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
                on sets of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in X
              be two points. Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P_{x,y} X
            %p
              for the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(0) = x
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(1) = y
            %p
              Then
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"} homotopy relative boundary
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathHomotopyRelativeBoundary"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{x,y}X
            %p
              The corresponding set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              is denoted
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(x,y)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    (P_{x,y}X)/\sim
                    \\,.
          %p
            Recall the operations on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+concatenation"} path concatenation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_2 \cdot \gamma_1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+reversion"} path reversion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\gamma}
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+paths"} constant paths
          #ConcatenationOfHomotopyClassesOfPaths.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+concatenation"} concatenation
                of
                = succeed "-classes" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"} homotopy relative boundary
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+concatenation"} path concatenation
              descends to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"} homotopy relative boundary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y, z \in X
              there is a function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Π
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Π
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Π
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(x,y)
                    \\times
                    Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(y,z)
                    \&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;
                    Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(x,z)
                    \\\
                    ([\gamma_1], [\gamma_2])
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    [\gamma_2] \cdot [\gamma_1] \coloneqq  [\gamma_2 \cdot \gamma_1]
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Moreover,
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  this composition operation is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
                  in that for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z,w \in X
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi γ
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Π
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma_1] \in Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(x,y)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma_2] \in Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(y,z)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma_3] \in Hom_{\Pi_1(X)})(z,w)
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [\gamma_3] \cdot ([\gamma_2]\cdot [\gamma_1])
                        \\;=\;
                        ([\gamma_3] \cdot [\gamma_2]) \cdot [\gamma_1]
              %li
                %p
                  this composition operation is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unital
                  with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+elements"} neutral elements
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+paths"} constant paths
                  in that for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma] \in Hom_{\Pi_1(X)}(x,y)
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi const
                          %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
