          #UniversalCoveringRealLineOfCircle.num_example
            %h6#example_18 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
                of the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %p
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplyConnectedEuclideanSpace"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringOfCircleByRealLine"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\exp(2 \pi i(-)) \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^1 \longrightarrow S^1
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalCoveringSpaceUniqueUpToIsomorphism"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
          %h3#Monodromy Monodromy
          %p
            Since the lift of a path through a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            is unique once the lift of the starting point is chosen (lemma
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringSpacePathLifting"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            over its endpoints. By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
            of covering spaces as in example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringSpacesHomotopyLifting"}
            this function only depends on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            of the path under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+relative+boundary"} homotopy relative boundary
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of the base space on sets, called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+representation"} groupoid representation
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidRepresentation"}
            below). In particular, associated with any homotopy-class of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop"} loop
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            of the fiber over the loop’s basepoint with itself, hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            of the covering space. It is a measure for how the covering space fails to be globally trivial.
          %p
            In fact the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
            (prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalTheoremOfCoveringSpaces"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            representation characterizes the covering spaces completely and faithfully. This means that covering spaces may be dealt with completely with tools from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} below
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
