            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Rep(\mathcal{G}) = Hom_{Grpd}( \mathcal{G} , Core(\mathcal{C})  )
                    \\,.
            %p
              Consider the injection functor of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
              from lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopingGroupoidEquivalence"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inc
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    inc
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\underset{i \in \pi_0(\mathcal{G})}{\sqcup} B G_i
                    \\overset{}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathcal{G}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HmotopiesWithMorphismsHorizontaComposition"}
              the pre-composition with this constitutes a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi inc
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    inc^\ast \;\colon\; Hom( \mathcal{G}, \mathcal{C} ) \longrightarrow Hom( \underset{i \in \pi_0(\mathcal{G})}{\sqcup} B G_i, \mathcal{C} )
            %p
              and by combining lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopingGroupoidEquivalence"}
              with lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HorizontalCompositionWithHomotopyIsNaturalTransformation"}
              this is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductGroupoid"}
              the groupoid on the right is the product groupoid as claimed.
          #CoveringSpaceMonodromy.num_defn
            %h6#definition_20 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
                of a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{p}{\to} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalGroupoid"}
            %p Define a groupoid homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fib
                      %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fib_E
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\Pi_1(X)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Core(Set)
            %p
              to the groupoid core of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              (example
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidRepresentation"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+representation"} groupoid representation
              (example
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidRepresentation"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  to a point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  assign the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(\{x\}) \in Set
              %li
                %p
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path"} path
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                  connecting
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \coloneqq \gamma(0)
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \coloneqq \gamma(1)
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  assign the function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(\{x\}) \longrightarrow p^{-1}(\{y\})
                  which takes
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat x \in p^{-1}(\{x\})
                  to the endpoint of a path
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \gamma
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  which lifts
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                  through
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  with starting point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \gamma(0) = \hat x
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi p
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi p
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mover
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                %mo =
                                %mover
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↦
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        p^{-1}(x) &amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; p^{-1}(y)
                        \\\
                        (\hat x = \hat \gamma(0)) &amp;\mapsto&amp; \hat \gamma(1)
                        }
                        \\,.
            %p
              This construction is well defined for a given representative
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              due to the unique path-lifting property of covering spaces (lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringSpacePathLifting"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              in the given homotopy class of paths due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringSpacesHomotopyLifting"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
              and hence is indeed a homomorphism of groupoids (a functor).
          #FunctorialExtractingHomotopy.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_14 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (extracting
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorial
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              between two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi i
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi i
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_i \overset{p_i}{\to} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon E_1 \to E_2
              which respects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              in that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E_1 &amp;&amp; \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; E_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{p_1}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_2}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"}> commutes
              , then the component functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
